course: dictionary
lesson: 11149
title: Wildflowers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wildflower is a flower that grows naturally, without being planted by people. Its seeds are carried by wind, animals or water to new places, so wildflowers appear on their own in fields, hedges, roadsides and woods. Wild means not grown or controlled by people, like a wild animal.
explain: Look at the sentence: «Children play with wildflowers everywhere.» The word everywhere is a clue. It tells you wildflowers are found in many places, not only in gardens. When you meet a new word, read the words around it.
explain: Wildflowers matter for wildlife. «Long grass, wildflowers and a log pile give homes to insects, frogs and hedgehogs.» A wild corner holds more life than a tidy lawn. Wildflower meadows help bees and butterflies, so a wild patch is good for nature.
fact: A wildflower is a flower that grows naturally, without being planted by people.
fact: Wildflowers can be found in fields, hedges, roadsides and woods.
fact: Wildflower meadows help bees and butterflies.
fact: Some wildflowers are protected, so the countryside code says do not pick them.
fact: Children play games with wildflowers: blowing a dandelion clock to «tell the time», and hunting for a lucky four-leaf clover.
exercise: What is a wildflower? | A flower that only grows in shops | *A flower that grows naturally, without being planted by people | A flower made of paper | A flower planted in a garden by a gardener
exercise: Which of these helps bees and butterflies? | *Wildflower meadows | Tidy, cut lawns | Plastic flowers | Concrete car parks
exercise: «Children play with wildflowers everywhere.» What does everywhere mean here? | Only in winter | Only in the shop | Hidden underwater | *In many places
test: Which wildflower do children hunt for to find a lucky plant? | Buttercup | Dandelion | Plantain | *Clover
test: Why should you not pick some wildflowers? | It makes them sing | They turn into trees | *Some are protected, so the countryside code says leave them | They only grow in winter
exam: Which sentence shows that wildflowers are not planted by people? | Children plant wildflowers every spring | Wildflowers are sold in shops only | *Wildflowers grow naturally, without being planted by people | Gardeners plant wildflowers in tidy rows
